 "descripcion": "A green branch on a pole meant fresh ale for sale. Then the village ale-taster came to check it.\n\nPart 3: {when_next}.\nWould her ale pass?\n\n#history #medieval #middleages #historyfacts #shorts",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "The branch means fresh ale for sale. It's called an ale-stake.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Soon, a man in a good coat knocks on the door.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "He's the ale-taster, chosen by the village court.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "He checks three things: the taste, the price, and the jug.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "The price is set by law, and it follows the price of grain.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "And the jug must be the official size, never smaller.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Agnes pours. He drinks. He frowns.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "Did her ale pass? Part three, {when_next}.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
